ray  so that's what you have it won't be  perfect but that's fine so place this in  the freezer and allow it to set with the  remaining ingredients take one teaspoon  of cocoa powder and just mix it up and  I'll press it down into a really small  block what I want you to do now is to  cover this up and place this in the  freezer and let it set as well and we  will be using this for the second recipe  as we are waiting for the crust is set  in the freezer let's move on to making  the cheesecake  the ingredients you need are 1 cup of  whole cashew nuts soaked overnight and  drained 2 tablespoons of melted coconut  oil 2 tablespoons of lemon juice which  equals to 1 small lemon or half of a  large lemon 2 tablespoons of honey and  half a teaspoon of pure vanilla extract  melt the pure coconut oil using a double  boiler again we will be needing our food  processor what you'll need to do is to  pre-soak your cashew nuts overnight or  at least up to four hours the first step  is to grind the cashew nuts  and now just add your lemon juice  coconut oil 2 tbsp of honey you have a  teaspoon of vanilla extract and just  blend it again what you'll have is a  white creamy texture and this is your  cheesecake remove the muffin tray from  your freezer and top it up with your  cheesecake what we want to do now is to  place this back into the freezer and  you'll find a layer the mixed berries  sauce it's so fruity and the sweetness  will seep into the cheesecake the  ingredients you'll need are 2/3 cup of  frozen berries thawed and mashed which  is about 100 gram and 1 teaspoon of  honey mix the honey and berries in a pan  under low heat for one to two minutes we  do not want to be cooking it so Allah  you mix berries to cool down once it's  cool add it to the final layer of a  cheesecake and place it back into the  freezer and finally place this in the  freezer for four to six hours or  overnight all we need to do now is to  remove the cheesecakes from the silicone  muffin tray which should be easy  this mini buried cheesecake is perfect  for the festive season in fact all year  round each one of them has 306 point six  calories it's packed full of good  calories from your nuts coconut milk and  honey so indulge in them in moderation  we all know a dessert menu is never  complete without having chocolate in it  so what I have here a chocolate fudge  mousse to die for they are absolutely  delicious they make you feel so guilty  but so satisfied at the same time I have  previously shown you how to make a  healthy chocolate mousse dessert with  this recipe we want to add a little bit  more texture by adding some chocolate  fudge so let's start by making the  chocolate mousse the ingredients you'll  need are 1 block of silken tofu which is  about 300 gram one block of dark  chocolate about 100 gram and just 2 tbsp  of milk so the first step is to break  your chocolate bar into pieces and melt  using a double boiler you can choose to  use a food processor but I prefer my  smoothie blender add the silken tofu and  dark chocolate into the blender and  blend it up if you find that your  mixture is too thick you can just add a  splash of milk not too much and blend it  again and this is what you'll have a  thick chocolaty mix pour the mixture  into 5 small dessert glasses what I have  here are small recycable wine glasses so  let's place these desserts in the fridge  for 4 to 6 hours or overnight for them  to sat in the Sun of the video I've  asked you to store  quarter of your cheese crust away and  we've added a little bit of cocoa powder  onto it so remove that from the freezer  what we want to do now is to slice them  up into really small nuts and that will  be your chocolate fudge just take the  chocolate fudge and top it up onto your  chocolate mousse dessert the recipe is  for 5 surveys each serving has one  hundred and sixty eight point seven  calories at a small ribbon and they are  perfect for the season Cheers  and finally I have to share with you my  comfort food which is a Malaysia  favorite dessert called pooper cha-cha  Boober means porridge cha-cha I am not  too sure what that means  Boober ChaCha is like rice pudding in  the western country but is made of  healthy ingredients such as pumpkins  sweet potatoes ginger and coconut milk  so the ingredients you will need to make  Boober ChaCha  are 300 gram of sweet potato sliced into  small cubes 300 gram of fresh pumpkin  sliced into small cubes as well 70 gram  of tapioca pearls of sago 35 gram of  Chinese brown sugar bar 200 ml of  coconut milk which is about half a can  about 400 ml of water and 1 small slice  of ginger root crushed the first step is  to boil the pumpkin and sweet potato in  a large pot for 20 to 30 minutes until  tender  in the mean time so the tapioca pearls  in water for 10 to 15 minutes and  drained  once that's cooked just drain the water  off and just live enough water for the  brown sugar to dissolve add your brown  sugar and your crushed ginger in and  just stir it and allow your brown sugar  to dissolve reduce the heat at your  tapioca pearls or sago and stir well and  finally and your half a can of coconut  milk for the rich creamy texture and now  just stir it and allow it to simmer for  10 minutes  and the low heat what you just made are  five servings of uber ChaCha and each  serving only has 100 94.3 calories and  do you serve it in your favorite bowl we  can serve it hot or cold but I prefer it  hard especially  because the weather is getting so cold  right now I understand there are a lot  of negative remarks in regards to sugar  this brown sugar bars are actually made  from unrefined cane sugar and according  to Chinese medical experts this brown  sugar bus provides wonders throughout  the woman's body improve blood  circulation and relief pain  it's especially beneficial to women who  has just given birth or have an  irregular menstrual cycle you can buy  them in any Asian stores they are high  in calories therefore we have to consume  them in moderation I like that in my  dessert because it makes me feel really  good especially when the weather is so  cool outside and it's good to your tummy  with coconut milk it's very rich in  vitamins and minerals it's a great dairy  substitute it's very commonly used in  Asia but they are very high in calories  again we have to consume all these  healthy food in moderation so do try my  booger ChaCha out and let me know  whether you like it or not  remember healthy food does not mean low  in calories so enjoy them in moderation  as part of your balanced diet make them  for your family make them for your  friends let me know what you think in  the comments below and just enjoy this  beautiful time of the year for new  fitness food and motivational videos  please like share and subscribe to my  You Tube channel and website do you  follow me on Facebook Instagram and  Twitter to stay connected with me thanks  guys  [Music]

